---
description: DylKit app workflow — checks before a PR and where the conventions live
alwaysApply: true
---

Before opening or updating a PR, run `./run dev checks` (SwiftLint, `dyl-lint`, and `release-kit check`) and fix what it reports. Don't restate lint rules in code or docs; the findings explain themselves. Use `// lint:allow <rule>: <reason>` only for a verified benign hit.

Never take focus on Dylan's Mac. Launch apps only with `open -g`, which is all `./run dev relaunch` and `./run dev capture` do. Never use `osascript` (AppleScript `activate`, System Events keystrokes or menu clicks), `open` without `-g`, the app binary run directly, `open -a Simulator`, or a capture that raises a window. If a check needs any of those, it doesn't run on his Mac: say what's unverified. The same rule applies to prompts you write for other agents.

Conventions live in the skills under `.cursor/skills`: `apple-dev-loop`, `apple-release`, `swift-concurrency-io`, `liquid-glass-chrome`, `swiftui-views`, `swiftui-viewmodels`, `app-logging`, `ui-screenshot-tests` and `whats-ready`.
